ict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Tag filter facet list is static (built from seed tags), not derived from current product tags\", \"actual\": \"After adding tag \\\"qa-fresh-tag\\\" (and \\\"qa-lighting-renamed\\\") to the existing Philips Hue Starter Kit — a change that is live, since keyword search \\\"qa-fresh-tag\\\" returns that product and its detail page lists the tag — the /products advanced tag filter still lists only the original 35 seed tags; \\\"qa-fresh-tag\\\" and \\\"qa-lighting-renamed\\\" are absent, so the new tag cannot be selected as a filter. Conversely removed tags remain selectable and now return nothing (selecting \\\"ambiance\\\" → \\\"0 products found\\\"). Same for tags on newly created products (qa-desk/qa-lighting were never offered).\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Created \\\"QA Zen Desk Lamp\\\" with Tags field \\\"qa-desk, qa-lighting\\\"; detail page shows both tags as chips, and searching \\\"QA-LIGHTING\\\" on /products returns exactly that product (\\\"1 product found\\\").\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Edited Philips Hue tags from \\\"lighting, smart-home, ambiance, automation\\\" to \\\"smart-home, qa-lighting-renamed, qa-fresh-tag\\\" (kept one, renamed one, removed two, added one). Detail page shows exactly the 3 new tags; search \\\"qa-fresh-tag\\\" → 1 result (Philips Hue); search \\\"ambiance\\\" (removed tag) → \\\"0 products found\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Admin form category is a single-select with exactly Tech Gadgets/Home Goods/Fitness. Created \\\"QA Zen Desk Lamp\\\" with Home Goods → appears on /category/home (4 items) with badge \\\"Home\\\", and on its detail page category badge is Home; not present in tech/fitness listings.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Category filter on /products: Tech Gadgets→3 (Samsung, MacBook, Sony), Home Goods→3 (Breville, Philips Hue, Dyson), Fitness→3 (Bowflex, Theragun, Peloton); count text updates to \\\"3 products found\\\" each time.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"/products lists 9 products; each article exposes name (h3), category badge, price, rating value (e.g. 4.8), brief description, img, and an external purchase link (e.g. https://example.com/sony-xm5).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Sort price-asc gave 199→2495 ascending; price-desc gave 2495→199; Top Rated gave 4.9→4.4 descending; newest is default. Min rating 4.5+ reduced 9→8 (all ≥4.5). Dragging price slider set range $0–$1250 → 5 products, all ≤$1250.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Admin changes are in-memory only and are lost on reload/revisit\", \"actual\": \"Created \\\"QA Zen Desk Lamp\\\" (Home Goods, featured) and \\\"QA Minimal Product\\\", unfeatured Sony, and changed Philips Hue tags — all visible in the running session. After reloading (navigating to http://localhost:6001/product/philips-hue-starter-kit) the app reset to the 9 seeded products: /products shows \\\"9 products found\\\" with no QA products, Philips Hue tags reverted to lighting/smart-home/ambiance/automation, and Sony is featured again. localStorage is empty (no persistence layer).\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All 9 seeded products show exactly one category badge (Tech/Home/Fitness) and category counts sum 3+3+3=9. Admin form category is a single-value select offering only Tech Gadgets, Home Goods, Fitness; created product got exactly one (Home).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Tags wireless+coffee → 2 results (Sony has wireless, Breville has coffee: OR semantics, each result has ≥1 selected tag). Adding category=Tech narrowed to 1 (Sony), count \\\"1 product found\\\". Earlier rating≥4.5 and price ≤$1250 filters also only returned conforming products.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Publish validation only checks name + short description; incomplete/invalid products are accepted\", \"actual\": \"Submitting the admin form with only Name=\\\"QA Minimal Product\\\" and a short description created and published the product (empty full review, empty image URL, empty affiliate link, no specification rows, price $0). Re-editing it and saving price=\\\"-50\\\" and affiliate link=\\\"not-a-valid-url\\\" also saved successfully — the admin list now shows \\\"-$50\\\" for that product. Only a fully empty form is rejected (\\\"Please fill in all required fields\\\"); rating is bounded 0-5 solely by the native number input max attribute.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-22\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"/product/does-not-exist-123 → \\\"Product Not Found\\\" message + Browse All Products link, 0 product cards. /category/bogus-cat → \\\"Category Not Found\\\", 0 product cards. No unrelated product data shown.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Category, sort, min-rating and price-range changes all re-rendered the grid, order and \\\"N products found\\\" count instantly with no navigation/reload (URL stayed /products).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking the Sony card name on /products navigated to /product/sony-wh-1000xm5 showing that product; card image is wrapped in the same href=\\\"/product/sony-wh-1000xm5\\\" anchor.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each card has a \\\"Buy Now\\\" anchor with target=_blank rel=noopener to the product's own retailer URL; clicking Sony's opened new tab https://example.com/sony-xm5.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Category selector on the category page is inert\", \"actual\": \"On /category/fitness the filter bar offers a category select (options All/Tech Gadgets/Home Goods/Fitness). Selecting \\\"Home Goods\\\" and then \\\"Tech Gadgets\\\" left everything unchanged: URL stayed /category/fitness, heading/category.name stayed \\\"Fitness\\\", the select still read \\\"Fitness\\\", and the grid still showed only Bowflex, Theragun, Peloton. On /products the same control works, so the failure is specific to category pages.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"/product/sony-wh-1000xm5 shows name \\\"Sony WH-1000XM5\\\", category badge Tech, rating 4.8, price $399, brief description, 446-char full review, 4 tags (headphones, wireless, noise-cancelling, premium), 5 specs (driver size, battery, weight, bluetooth, ANC), product image, and Buy Now action to https://example.com/sony-xm5.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Seeded tags are topically relevant: Sony WH-1000XM5 (Tech) → headphones, wireless, noise-cancelling, premium; Peloton Bike+ (Fitness) → cardio, cycling, smart-equipment, subscription; Samsung → flagship/smartphone; Breville (Home) → coffee/espresso. Category badge and tags match between list cards, tag filter facets and detail pages.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Peloton Bike+: homepage $2,495, category page Fitness/$2,495, products list Fitness/$2,495/4.6/\\\"Premium connected fitness bike…\\\", detail page identical name/category/price/rating/description plus full 462-char review and 5 specs shown untrunc